# tasks/events.jsonl is an append-only log — a standard textual 3-way
# merge (or a human/agent resolving a conflict by picking one side) can
# silently drop a real, already-merged line. This happened for real on
# 2026-09-21 (commit 61473f7, "auto-resolved: prefer PR branch", dropped
# dotfiles-tsk-dispatch-launcher's event). tasks/git-merge-jsonl-union.py
# always resolves a conflict here by taking the union of both sides,
# deduplicated by event_id and sorted by ts — see that script and
# setup.sh (which registers the `jsonl-union` driver name via `git
# config`; a merge driver referenced here without the matching local
# `git config merge.jsonl-union.driver` falls back to git's default
# textual merge, silently losing this protection).
tasks/events.jsonl merge=jsonl-union
